(a) The owner of a short-term rental shall designate a short-term rental agent on its application for a short-term rental permit. A property owner may serve as the short-term rental agent. Alternatively, the owner may designate a natural person as his or her agent who is over age 18 and is customarily present at a location within the city for purposes of transacting business.
(b) The duties of the short-term rental agent are to:
(1) Be reasonably available to handle any problems arising from use of the short-term rental unit;
